{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/639651-the-666-plot-hooks-for-demon-the-fallen","id":639651,"title":"The 666 Plot Hooks for Demon the Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-25T17:39:18-07:00","id":639651,"title":"The 666 Plot Hooks for Demon the Fallen","content":"Got an idea for a game? to start up a campaing? post it here :P and yeah, i just put 666 to make it sound more Ominous xD. the idea its to make as many plot hooks as you guys want","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T19:04:52-07:00","id":639700,"title":"","content":"No prob with the 666. Is like the 1001 Domains thread in V:tR's session.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to start a very simple one, I can actually even need some ideas to expand. The characters are some of the very first escapees from Hell (I'm not using quite the canon and freely pushing the 6th Maelstrom to present day), and the chronicle is about them deciding what to do with the world and their lives as the ones to help to shape the &quot;nascent&quot; demonic society and the world at large.<br /> <br /> The theme is Shaping the Future, and the mood is of Self-Sustaining Expectations. Hope can truly shine, but hatred can grew completely unbound. Any choice creates ripples and reflects back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T14:55:25-07:00","id":640673,"title":"","content":"-A local anti-government terrorist group is starting to become more powerful as local police officers are being killed in the name of God and freedom. It appears that their messianic leader appeals to downtrodden men who are angry at the world and willing to fight his battles for him. But the truth is that if it weren't for the Faustian Demon who is manipulating him into believing he's been chosen by God, this cowardly, entitled man would be a mess. So what do the players do? Join the terrorists to get their own piece of the pie or usurp the Demon? Fight through an angry milita to take them down? Or take advantage of the grieving families?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:39:59-07:00","id":640891,"title":"","content":"- A mysterious Relic of unknown materials and origin appears in the Demon's territory. Cultists one by one (from the Demon's or others) start disappearing when they obtain this Relic. The Demon (or Demons) investigate the Relic and it turns out to be a gateway from somewhere beyond Creation. And the Demon/Demons encounter the denizens of this outer realm. The Heirophants, Demons to some, Angels to others, Explorers from beyond experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T20:05:59-07:00","id":642399,"title":"","content":"From Redford_Blade in that other Demon thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=606674#post606674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hapxier, one of your closest allies from the War, has recently reached out to you, asking for your help in a nearby city. When you attempt to respond to Hapxier's request, nothing happens; it is as if Hapxier no longer exists. Do you set off to follow the clues you picked up from Hapxier's last message? Has the former angel been consumed, or are they hidden away in a place where even your mental summons cannot reach?<br /> <br /> While reading a magazine, watching the news, or browsing the internet, you notice an article about a group of mortal archaeologists pulling a stone obelisk from the sea floor. The article makes wry comments about the lost city of Atlantis, but you know full well what the obelisk is. After all, you helped to put it there. What is it, and what does it mean that the mortals have found it now?<br /> <br /> While walking through your city or town, you notice that the children have been giving you odd glances out of the corners of their eyes. They think they are being discreet, but as children, they have yet to master subtlety. The adults don't seem to pay you any more attention than normal, only the children. Are the little ones being co-opted by your enemies to spy on you? Have rumors of your true nature started to spread? Or is there some utterly mundane reason for their attention?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:18:38-07:00","id":649166,"title":"","content":"A young person of importance to the characters -or their allies- is kidnapped in clear defiance to their powerbase. Following the trial they find out that she is going to be sacrificed in some ritual. A fellow Fallen, the one behind the scheme and rite, happily offers to release her as a token of friendship in exchange for alliance. He turns out to be a servant of one of the Earthbound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7557-profeta-del-pesar","name":"Profeta del Pesar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:30:05-07:00","id":649315,"title":"","content":"I had a rather weird idea after reading Devil's Due, not long after it came out. Given that this was quite a long time ago, it's possible that I've completely misremembered what was in the actual book, but the plot idea stuck with me.<br /> <br /> I remember thinking that the way the book portrayed creating a demonic player character, sounded a lot like the summoner had carved a piece of the demon itself to have it weak enough to possess a human host without immediately consuming it. I'd started thinking about what might have happened to the rest of the demon. Since demons are not physical creatures the way humans are, could what was left in the Abyss still retain (or reform/regain) consciousness? And then, if it did, what would happen to it when the Abyss was torn open in 1999?<br /> <br /> So then, you have the player character as the modern demon (created from what was left in the Abyss, having healed enough to have retained its consciousness/sense of identity, escaped, and now possessing a human host), and an NPC adversary made up of the part of the Demon that had been summoned in the Dark Ages, having done god knows what to stay free and alive in the present day.<br /> <br /> Obviously it's a little too single-player focused to be a group plot hook, but it might make an interesting thread to weave into an existing chronicle. And offer a different sort of adversary for the group. How do you fight someone who is essentially you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T18:13:02-07:00","id":649582,"title":"","content":"An idea I've had kicking around for a while for a game. Your group hears about a group of fallen that are going to attempt the unthinkable, they each have assembled cults numbering in the thousands funneling every ounce of faith they can generate into themselves. They are just a few steps away from creating a ritual that will do something none of the fallen have been able to do since before their time in hell. They are going to try to create a new Eden completely from scratch, to form a completely new seed that may grow into a completely new realm. The group has heard that at least 7 fallen from each visage of each house are part of the endeavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T06:54:03-07:00","id":657814,"title":"","content":"Hell Block:<br /> The characters awaken in the bodies of convicts who were part of a prison riot. They have swapped one prison for another.<br /> <br /> But as they merge fully with their new hosts and learn and understand where they are to get a stark look at what prison for humans is like in the WoD and stand shoulder to shoulder with some of the worst.<br /> some wanting freedom, some awaiting their execution, others running rampant and spreading more terror and pain from within these bars and others searching for redemption.<br /> <br /> as their powers in Lores in crease and they find their new path in the world do they long and plan to escape or make the prison theirs?<br /> <br /> Demons can choose to punish the wicked, redeem, prove the innocence of those held falsely or rule the worst of mankind and forge them for what is to come. War!<br /> <br /> Add to it the prison was built on a site of an old pre fall fortress and is built with some of the original foundations and fortifications of concepts and resonates well enough to correspond to lores and powers of protection and defense...what do they do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:04:09-07:00","id":657825,"title":"","content":"We Dont Need no Education:<br /> <br /> (Yes you do, because that's a double negative)<br /> <br /> The characters awaken in the host bodies of children and young teens. It appaers they are the only survivors of a terrible crash involving the school bus.<br /> <br /> They each have partial amnesia due to the concussions received to the host bodies prior to possession. They have the chance to be cared for and healed by medical staff, praised as little miracles by the local media, hugged and held with oceans of grateful tears from their parents and witness the loss of their friends and be centre stage in the misery and pain of the families of those less fortunate.<br /> <br /> The home lives can be as good or as awful as you wish. Either way they have school. Bullies, teachers, homework, peer pressure, but it's not long till summer vaycay.<br /> <br /> They each start to remember everything about what they were, before, during and after the fall. And now they have perfect cover, possible thralls in parents and friends. praise and worship for being little miracles and even the chance to carve out a little slice of heaven or continue their path from the wake of hell.<br /> <br /> add to it the Phys Ed teacher is a little...ok a lot of stangeness to him.<br /> The Bus driver who also survives is arrested as its uncovered the crash was done deliberately and he killed himself after admitting he did for the Angels.<br /> and the Psychiatrist brought into the school to help the children in their grief has singled them out and is taking a very keen interest in them all points to something...but what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:52:15-07:00","id":657882,"title":"","content":"Coyote UghLi:<br /> <br /> The Troupe have to cross the desert to get to where they need to go. It's a few days drive and honestly the whole trip has been one calamity after the other. There was a mix up with the plane tickets. It took a day to get a rental car (as all the others were booked out months in advance for a RPconvention of all things) and some punk actually dated to steal their stuff from the dodgey motel that had 'Bates' written all over it. <br /> <br /> And now the rentals engine has exploded under the heat of the sun and it's still days of travel.<br /> <br /> But then a spot of luck. Another traveller and also former inmate of the abyss can help them. Meet Jeff, local know it all and professional courier of people seeking a new life elsewhere. The charming Devil and Coyote says he's heading their way and can give a lift. Plus he knows how to avoid all the big bad out here.<br /> <br /> It wasnt an easy ride. Crooked cops, an armed holdup at the diner (where they still didnt cook your eggs right) and a small bunch of malevolent bikers looking for who ripped them off and gutted their leader the night before.<br /> <br /> but the end is in sight.<br /> <br /> accept for that feeling that something is very wrong and someone is trying your 'name'.<br /> <br /> Jeff confesses. There's a bunch of hungry Raveners lead by UghLi the Desolator of Flesh after the Troupe. They've been using the disteactions, corrupt cops, bikers and everything else to force them to use their lores so they can come in after and learn about them. Learn what they can do and maybe even take a guess at who they really are so they can pick which ones they want and hsve a hearty and filling meal.<br /> <br /> Jeff is their patsy, their plant, their decoy. He's enslaved to them and has little to no choIce. He says he feels bad and can get them to where they need yo go. But only, only if the troupe stay and destriy the hunting Raveners hellbent on devouring them.<br /> <br /> that way jeff will be free. He cant help directly, otherwise they'll destroy him. He says he's pretty sure he knows parts of their name/natures too. Which he'll give once they are taken down. If...they help him. Otherwise...well...he might just let the Raveners have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:50:12-07:00","id":657929,"title":"","content":"Possession is 9.99 10ths of the Lore:<br /> <br /> The gang have been hunting down a group of rogue demons that havent identified themselves to the court of the damned. They've been closing the gap and readying to spring their trap on the interlopers and something...very weird happens when they finally confront them. A flash of blinding brillIant light nearly fuses out their souls/spirit/whateva.<br /> <br /> when they open their eyes, they dont recognise where they are, or who they are. Or the names others seem to be calling them. They know full well who they were, who their hosts, thralls and positions in the courts were...but they dont know these bodies.<br /> <br /> After playing and spending xp on Attributes, Abilities. Building up their influences, thralls and devotees they now are in new bodies.<br /> Bodies that are sick, weak, unnoticed, unknown, forgetton and deemed worthless by the society around them. Lives that have been trodden down to lower than dirt.<br /> what?! They have to build themselves back up?!<br /> That's too harsh!<br /> But wait, for some reason these new hosts seem more acclimatised to their Lores and they are all higher than they were. Plus their Torment is lower.<br /> weird! But wait! What about their old bodies?<br /> Holy carp! They are walking around! Still?! Buwah??!!<br /> It's worse. There's another Fallen in their old hosts posing as them! What's really insiduous is that they seem to be freeing folk of the thralldom and contracts. They are also undoing and paying back every wrong they've done. Every duplicitous act, every con, trick, death, and devious plot they are making or giving retribution for and asking for forgiveness.<br /> <br /> what's really adding salt to the wounds is that these Devilish Redeemers seem to be taking on the pre fall roles of the Troupes characters and acting on them in new ways. Of course this is upsetting all those plans, ploys and hard won victories you've been building up and giving others a different perception of you altogether.<br /> <br /> what to do? Especially when the local insane alley drunk turns up claiming to be the head of the Dragon ministry but no one is listening.<br /> <br /> How many of the court are being Redeemed in such away? Do the characters actually end up liking their new bodies and hightened power? Do they go after their old bodies? Do they try to out do the Redeemer imposters by proving they are who they say are by taking on their prefall roles better? Or do they get desperare for what they've lost recently rather than originally and go street fight to make the imposters regret messing with them and reclaim their hosts?<br /> <br /> What do they do when the Devilish Redeemers just smile and say &quot;of course, you may have your host back. It's yours, it always was.&quot; Do they continue the path the Redeemers have made for them with its reflections of former angelic glory for human kind or go back to who they were before the redeemers tried to 'help'?<br /> <br /> Hosts get Jacked<br /> Old roles realised and new foundations for them already in place to have a resurgence if chosen<br /> or slip back into old habits. It's up to you once you get it back...or dont","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:55:43-07:00","id":660063,"title":"","content":"-It seems that local Thralls (including the PCs') are dropping like flies in a series of &quot;accidents&quot;. Is it divine intervention, a coincidence or is something else behind this mess?<br /> <br /> -A pack of Black Spiral Dancers (or Formori) have discovered how useful a Demon's faith and torment can be. So now it's a game of wolf-and-mouse to avoid them (and don't even bother asking the Garou for help) and make sure word doesn't come out to the rest of their foul kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T17:16:50-07:00","id":660123,"title":"","content":"There's word that a young girl is performing miracles and is right for thralldom.<br /> Several local key players and Antagonists are going after her. It's a race against time and her potential faith is worth getting bloody and violent for.<br /> <br /> Are you going after her for yourself, your master, or to save her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T17:23:43-07:00","id":660125,"title":"","content":"Sightings have been reported of a young gang member somehow is armed with 'sound of deaths symphony'. A weapon forged by infamous Slayer from prefall. Cut from the slayers own pattern of creation. <br /> <br /> It is a legend of its own right and is currently in the form of a desert eagle pistol. The gang member has already become gang leader and taken out his competition and leaders of other gangs. Anyone that steps up, gets put down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T18:04:32-07:00","id":662494,"title":"","content":"There's a new biblical era artifact exhibit at the local museum. One in particular is King Soloman's Box that gives off a powerful energy that your kind can sense and is unable to be opened by the Mortals and their tools. But what is in it? Is Lucifier's soul really in there like the legends say and if so, what will the party do? Having a mixed faction party alone can cause plenty of problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T03:14:20-07:00","id":673041,"title":"","content":"It started off so simple.<br /> <br /> Well, as simple as a child kidnapping can be. Some mortal psycho snagged a little girl from the Evangelicals half a block over. Nothing to do with you and yours and there was a 'lesser' Earthbound to deal with when she went missing, so you didn't have the time to spare. Now that the local 'Court' has take care of it (you are still waiting for your reward), you have time to do more than just watch the story unfold in the news.<br /> <br /> Except the cops have tracked down the psycho. Except it wasn't just one guy, it appeared to be a mid-sized cult. And they were all dead. Around a ceremonial circle the mortal authorities are calling Satanic. One you recognise as a Summoning circle for a Fallen. It's been damaged it some kind of fight, probably because the binding didn't take and that's obscuring the newly Returnee's identity.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the girl is still missing.<br /> <br /> Good news is there is enough information left to identify some basic elements of it's rank. Lion imagery makes it clear which ministry it served in the Legion's, though not which Legion. The bad news is defiantly more abundant. These cultist weren't some inheritors of ancient secrets or some crazy whack jobs.They were hired guns, working to a plan &amp; a time table set by someone else. The cops didn't mention that. So now you got to figure out who set this thing up and find the Fallen who appears to have killed and mutilated her own summoners.<br /> <br /> The worse part is, you didn't figure out she was a Duke until you got to the crime scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}